    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάνδᾰλ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλανος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11.4
			</span></i>, Zeno 
				Med.
			 ap. Erot.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμβην</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				2.10
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μανδᾰλ-όω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυλαρώσας</span>
			; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μανδᾰλ-ωτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
				<i>with the bolt shot</i>, -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόν:
				εἶδος φιλήματος</span>, perh. kiss <i>with the tongue
				protruded</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Telecl.
				13
			</span></i>: hence, <i>lascivious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλος . . κατεγλωττισμένον καὶ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					132
				</span></i>
			.</div>
